<title>USA: Fed could add temporary reserves via system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed could add temporary reserves via system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve is likely to add temporary reserves to the banking system on Tuesday, analysts said.</p>
<p>Analysts said they calculated that the Fed had a &quot;small add need.&quot;</p>
<p>Also, Federal funds were trading at 5-9/16 percent, above the Fed's 5-1/2 percent target for the rate, in early dealings.</p>
<p>(( -- E. Freilich, North American Treasury Desk 212-859-1679))</p>
